    "turn_text": "Now, Ohioans become a caricature and he's baiting us. He's trying to bait people on the right to take up arms and the vast, vast, vast, vast, vast, vast, vast, vast, vast, vast majority of all of you won't take the bait. But the question is it only takes one or two people to slip up. and to take him literally, and then the Democrats will have a new cycle to run on for years. So that's the trick, is that if you got a 41 year old guy who tries to run over an 18 year old in his car, because that 18 year old is allegedly a MAGA extremist, even though he's not, then that's a momentary new cycle or something that kicks around conservative media for a couple of weeks. But if you have a incident like we saw at Charlottesville where one white guy ran over one white woman with his car, then that's a five year news cycle. And it described as racist, the greatest act of racism in modern times. So know what the media is trying to do. They're trying to create a climate. of not just a vision, but of civil war where the violent people are the maggas. And they totally ignore the 100 plus instances of left wing violence from over the summer. Same way they acted like the summer of love 2020 was mostly peaceful riding. That's the tactic. And the fault is always going to be of the Trump MAGA base. Barack Obama was out there claiming that racism to suppress American claims that racism is what's oppressing Americans opposition to Biden's deadly migration. You might be able to be right up for this at Breitbart. But he told a meeting of Hispanic realtors over the weekend in San Diego. Right now, the biggest fuel behind the Republican agenda is related to immigration and the fear. Somehow America's character is going to be chained to people of darker shades. There are too many of them here. That's right. We don't like the Browns. What is he talking about? It is so offensive that a guy who benefited so much from America's not racism. is still lecturing us on our racism. Hey,