er the Russian propaganda that was peddled on Facebook in 2016. He actually apologized for that. So, and then he funded, you know, acronym and courier with jobs. And he's been very China friendly. LinkedIn is the most China friendly American owned social media network, full stop. And so he's actually buddyed up with Chinese regulators. Some of these anecdotes are pretty unbelievable that Peter has in Red-handed on the China front. He also invited Jeffrey Epstein to a big event at MIT Media Lab. So pretty much a cross the board, not a good guy, and someone who's trying to use system to cheat. And you can store else on others to create this massive fund. And this fund is as far as we know, perhaps as much as $65 million. But maybe it's more, it's hard to know because the good information project, it only got their 501c3 status in April of 2022, that's this year. So this group, which is supposed to be 501c3, which means their tax exempt, they get this money, we don't know much it is, maybe it's tens of millions of dollars. And according to a whistleblower, a Harvard train, non-Trump backing guy named Preston Moore, who was unearthed on the Libs of TikTok account, and we've spoken to him, a Breitbart, Joel Pollack did, said that he was asked specifically to create content that would participate in the midterm elections. Now, I don't know if he's telling the truth, but I have no reason to believe based off of what he said that this isn't true. There's no reason to doubt him. So you've got a Harvard-trained guy who doesn't like Trump saying he was offered $400 by the Good Information Foundation to create anti-Trump, anti-Republican, anti-Maga content specifically to affect the midterms. That was what he said. And so this is textbook violation of 501c3 rules. and I have low expectations for the IRF so they'll do something about it. But I decided I would file a complaint because at a minimum it's a marker in the sand to note that the IRF is gonna add 87,000 new agents unless their Republicans can stop them. That they are ignoring what's clear corruption and clear election interference in their midst. And it seems like when it's such a slam dunk, I thought that as a citizen it would actually be a mistake if I didn't do it. And it would be purely out of fear of the IRS, which I do fear the IRS, but mostly that the waste my time. It's the not that I didn't think wrong or something. I'm very meticulous not doing stuff wrong, as far as the IRS goes. But they can potentially, if they get mad that I sent them a complaint, I guess they could waste a bunch of my time, which I'm hoping they don't. But it seems like one, we can't be afraid to do this stuff, because we can't be afraid of the IRS or else we're hanging in a very dark path. But when you've got a group that is funded by the biggest billionaires in town. And I was on Charlie Kirk's show when I talked about it yesterday and I, the way I described it is these groups, if they get shut down, they just change the name on the door and then the same money and the same people run these groups even more. Like they, it just goes on. This is very similar to what we were pouring on with Arabella advisors. If those of you want to look up some of our content on that. But 501c3 organizations are quote, absolutely prohibited from directly or indirectly participating in or intervening in any political campaign on behalf of or in opposition to any candidate for elected public office. Directly in contrast to what Preston Moore told us at Breitbart and when he said in his Libs of TikTok video. And we know how well funded they are, and we know that even if the IRS does an investigation and they should, we're not going to get the results until after the election. So this is potentially a business model that has been created by the Democrats to use. where you stand up an organization quickly, like a traveling circus, which is the way Charlie put it. And then you can use that traveling circus to essentially interfere in elections. And then if they're shut down, you just move the personnel in the cash to a different entity with a different name, Bob's your uncle. I find this be very disturbing as a citizen, not just as a right wing commentator and journalist, which of course, for that reason, sure, of course. doubly so. But just as a normal citizen, this is undermining our democracy in a major way. And unless Preston Moore is lying, then we've got these guys red-handed, you would think. But again, I don't have access type of information IRS has. And it is too recent that their 501c3 status was accepted for us to know exactly who's putting what money and where into that entity because it's going to lay of like a year and a half or so before you can see some of those disclosures. And a lot of the stuff that you would really want to see is aren't going to get disclosed anyway. So anyway, I put that complaint in, we wrote it up at Breitbart News, and I do not have my hope super high that anything big will come of it, but I did feel it important to put that marker in the sand, and that's what I did. So I thought you'd be interested to know, since I was on the front page at Breitbart, and I felt like I did want to bring it up on the show, and now I have. Our seems police is on, minority whip, and likely someone who will be in the leadership pretty high up if the Republicans take the Congress, which is almost guaranteed. Not quite. The Senate's much harder battle, but the House seems to be pretty well in hand at this point. So what are the Republicans going to do when they get there? We finally got some indication of what that will look like. Where else, Breitbart News. where a congressman laid out the commitment to America agenda with the exclusive story on that. We've had quite a number of follow-ups as well, which I recommend to you the audience. But let's hear what Congressman Scalise has to say on this and some other topics. Congressman, we'd have you back on. Tell us about the agenda, the commitment to America.",
