    "turn_text": "You've got to get back to restoring and respecting police, you know, and standing up to the defund the police movement, but also this no cash bail movement, because one of the other big problems we're seeing in most of our big cities is these prosecutors who won't even enforce laws. And so you grant money through that power, the purse, to say you don't get grants if you're defunding police or if you're not charging criminals with actual crimes and you're just letting them back out on the street against the laws. The law say the criminals should be in jail and DAs right now in some of these cities, you just saying, well, who cares? If it's a certain crime, we're just going to let them out. We're not going to charge them. And that's really what's crushing a lot of these cities driving crime through the roof, because criminals are paying attention to what these DAs are saying into them.",
